{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home.hbs — the homepage. Bands ported from
     NS-Design-System/templates/sections-home.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     THIS SITE IS NEW, and the homepage is written for that rather than
     pretending otherwise. A new site has almost no archive, so a homepage
     built around "browse our 200 lessons" renders as a set of empty shelves.
     The one thing it does have is a direction, so the page asks for the only
     commitment worth asking a first-time visitor for: an email address.

     Every band degrades to nothing when its data is absent — {{#get}} blocks
     carry an {{else}}, so a site with zero published posts still renders a
     complete page rather than a run of empty headings.

     THE HEADLINE COPY IS A GHOST SETTING, not a string in this file. Admin →
     Design → Site-wide. The defaults below are placeholders and are meant to
     be replaced; a headline hard-coded in a template is one the site owner
     cannot fix without a deploy.

     ⚠ One CTA band per page, at the end — NSDS's rule, and the reason the
     subscribe form appears twice here rather than three times.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{!-- ── HERO ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     .ns-hero--split makes .ns-band__inner a two-column grid: the words, then
     the mark. Below 64rem it collapses to one column with the WORDS FIRST —
     NSDS's own rule, and the reason the media slot is second in the source.

     The subscribe form is here rather than a button, because on a site with
     almost no archive the email address IS the conversion. A button to a
     portal costs a click and a modal before anyone can act.
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-hero ns-hero--split ns-band--dark ns-band--grid">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">

        <div>
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{#if @custom.hero_kicker}}{{@custom.hero_kicker}}{{else}}{{t "Learn Salesforce, properly"}}{{/if}}</span>

            <h1 class="ns-hero__title">
                {{#if @custom.hero_title}}{{@custom.hero_title}}{{else}}{{@site.title}}{{/if}}
            </h1>

            <p class="ns-hero__lede">
                {{#if @custom.hero_lede}}{{@custom.hero_lede}}{{else if @site.description}}{{@site.description}}{{/if}}
            </p>

            {{#if @site.members_enabled}}
                {{!-- data-members-form="subscribe" is Ghost's own hook: its
                     members script intercepts the submit, posts the address
                     and flips the elements marked data-members-success /
                     data-members-error. No JavaScript of ours, no action URL
                     to keep correct.

                     BOTH RESPONSE MESSAGES EXIST UP FRONT, hidden. A live
                     region created at the same moment as its message
                     announces nothing — the region has to be in the DOM
                     before the text lands in it.

                     .ns-cta-card__form carries `display:flex` and the
                     `flex: 1` on .ns-input, so the field and the button lay
                     out with no utility and no inline style. mt-6 is the one
                     thing NSDS has no class for here: .ns-hero__actions would
                     bring its own flex and fight the form's. --}}
                <form class="ns-cta-card__form mt-6" data-members-form="subscribe">
                    <label class="ns-visually-hidden" for="hero-email">{{t "Email address"}}</label>
                    <input id="hero-email" class="ns-input" type="email" name="email"
                           autocomplete="email" required
                           placeholder="{{t "you@example.com"}}" data-members-email>
                    <button class="ns-btn ns-btn--white ns-btn--lg" type="submit">
                        {{> "icons/paper-plane-tilt"}} {{t "Subscribe"}}
                    </button>
                </form>

                <p class="ns-field__help" data-members-success role="status" hidden>
                    {{t "Check your inbox — the confirmation link is on its way."}}
                </p>
                <p class="ns-field__error" data-members-error role="alert" hidden>
                    {{t "That did not work. Check the address and try again."}}
                </p>
            {{else}}
                <div class="ns-hero__actions">
                    <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--white ns-btn--lg" href="#latest">
                        {{> "icons/arrow-right"}} {{t "See what's here so far"}}
                    </a>
                </div>
            {{/if}}

            <span class="ns-hero__proof">
                {{#if @custom.hero_proof}}{{@custom.hero_proof}}{{else}}{{t "Free · no spam · unsubscribe any time"}}{{/if}}
            </span>
        </div>

        {{!-- The mark, on a loop. Second in the source so it lands UNDER the
             words when the grid collapses. See assets/css/theme/logo-sting.css
             for where the geometry comes from and why the theme draws this one
             thing itself. --}}
        <div class="ns-hero__media">
            {{> "logo-sting"}}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── WHAT HAPPENS NEXT ───────────────────────────────────────────────
     .ns-shipped is NSDS's "is this thing still alive" band — dated and
     time-ordered. On an established site it is a changelog; on this one it is
     the honest answer to "has anything been published yet", and it is real
     data rather than a promise. --}}
{{#get "posts" limit="5" include="tags" as |recent|}}
    {{#if recent}}
        <section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
            <div class="ns-band__inner">
                <div class="ns-band__head">
                    <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Still being written"}}</span>
                    <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Published recently"}}</h2>
                    <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "The curriculum is being built in public. This is what has landed most recently."}}</p>
                </div>

                <div class="ns-shipped">
                    {{#foreach recent}}
                        <a class="ns-shipped__row" href="{{url}}">
                            <span class="ns-shipped__date"><time datetime="{{date format="YYYY-MM-DD"}}">{{date format="D MMM"}}</time></span>
                            <span class="ns-shipped__kind">{{> "icons/plus-circle"}} {{#primary_tag}}{{name}}{{else}}{{t "New"}}{{/primary_tag}}</span>
                            <span class="ns-shipped__title">{{title}}</span>
                        </a>
                    {{/foreach}}
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    {{/if}}
{{/get}}

{{!-- ── LATEST ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The id is what the hero's second button targets. It stays on the section
     even when there are no posts, so the button never scrolls to nothing. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight" id="latest">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--between">
            <div>
                <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Writing"}}</span>
                <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Latest"}}</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="ns-band__actions">
                <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline ns-btn--sm" href="{{@site.url}}/archive/rss/">{{> "icons/rss"}} RSS</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        {{#get "posts" limit="6" include="authors,tags" as |posts|}}
            {{#if posts}}
                <div class="ns-blog-grid">
                    {{#foreach posts}}{{> "post-card"}}{{/foreach}}
                </div>
            {{else}}
                {{> "empty"
                    title=(t "Nothing published yet")
                    text=(t "The first lessons are being written. Subscribe below and they will reach you the day they go up.")}}
            {{/if}}
        {{/get}}
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── FOLLOW ALONG ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Renders only when the owner has actually filled in a handle — an empty
     row of placeholder icons is worse than no band at all. --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight ns-band--sunken">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--center">
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Elsewhere"}}</span>
            <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Follow along while it is built"}}</h2>
            <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "Work in progress gets posted as it happens — drafts, teardowns, and the parts that did not work."}}</p>
        </div>
        {{> "footer/social"}}
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── THE CLOSER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Exactly one CTA band, at the end. NSDS's rule, and the reason the page
     does not open with a subscribe form as well. --}}
{{#if @site.members_enabled}}
    <section class="ns-band ns-band--dark ns-band--grid">
        <div class="ns-band__inner">
            <div class="ns-cta">
                <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Know what happens next"}}</h2>
                <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "This site is at the beginning. Subscribe and you get every new lesson, roadmap and teardown as it ships — and a say in what gets written next."}}</p>
                <div class="ns-cta__actions">
                    <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--white ns-btn--lg" href="#/portal/signup" data-portal="signup">
                        {{> "icons/envelope"}} {{t "Subscribe"}}
                    </a>
                </div>
                <span class="ns-cta__fine">{{t "Free · no spam · unsubscribe any time"}}</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
{{/if}}
